      en: "The Carnegie Library in Victoria, Seychelles, was established in 1912 thanks to a grant of £2,500 from the Carnegie Trust. The neoclassical building features a colonnaded façade and a prominent pediment. It initially served as both a lending library and a museum. Over the decades, it accumulated a valuable collection of Creole literature and historical documents. In 1972, the library was transferred to the Ministry of Culture. It now houses over 20,000 books, including local heritage materials. The library underwent a comprehensive digital transformation in 2018.",
