      en: "The National Museum of History in Victoria, Mahé, founded in 1979, is Seychelles' premier historical institution, housed in a mid-19th century colonial building originally used as a customs house. Its permanent collection features over 2,000 artifacts spanning the pre-colonial, colonial, and post-independence eras. Highlights include traditional dugout canoes, plantation tools, and a rare collection of 18th-century navigational charts. A dedicated gallery examines the transatlantic slave trade and its abolition in 1835. The museum also holds original documents from the 1976 independence ceremony, including the constitution signed by Queen Elizabeth II. The research archive contains 15,000 photographs and manuscripts, making it a vital resource for historians. With 40,000 annual visitors, it serves as an educational hub for local schools and tourists alike.",
